# Site.css cache-bust version

Whenever you change `Styles/Site.css`, **always** bump the version in **both** places in the same edit:

1. **Header** in `Styles/Site.css` — top comment, e.g. `Rev: 20260722-1`
2. **Link** in `Site.Master` — `href="~/Styles/Site.css?v=20260722-1"`

## Format

`YYYYMMDD-n` (same as project docs: `Documentation/PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md`)

- `YYYYMMDD` = calendar date of the change (e.g. `20260722` = 22 Jul 2026)
- `n` = revision that day: start at `1`, then `2`, `3`… if CSS is changed again the same day

Do **not** leave an old `?v=` after CSS edits — browsers will keep serving cached CSS.
